From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Edwards <CFSworks@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:18:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: aggregator: Add "turing,pi2-nodes" compatible

Turing Pi 2 boards (v2.4 and v2.5) declare a "turing,pi2-nodes" GPIO
aggregator from device tree (sun8i-t113s-turing-pi2-v2.{4,5}.dts) to
expose the four node-power GPIOs to userspace as a single chardev for
bmcd. Add the compatible string so the driver binds without relying on
"driver_override".

Originally written by Sam Edwards <CFSworks@gmail.com>; rebased onto
v6.18.27, which kept the aggregator OF table layout unchanged but moved
the table to line 1637.

Link: https://github.com/turing-machines/BMC-Firmware/blob/master/tp2bmc/patches/linux/0002-gpio-aggregator-Add-turingmachines-tp2-nodes-compati.patch
(The original upstream patch, written 2023-05-20, carries no Signed-off-by;
the compatible string was "turingmachines,tp2-nodes" there.)
Signed-off-by: Sam Edwards <CFSworks@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Daniel Steinhauf <daniel@steinhauf.eu>
---
 drivers/gpio/gpio-aggregator.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/gpio-aggregator.c b/drivers/gpio/gpio-aggregator.c
index 17db07cf9..0aca5644b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-aggregator.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-aggregator.c
@@ -1654,6 +1654,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id gpio_aggregator_dt_ids[] = {
 	 * Add GPIO-operated devices controlled from userspace below,
 	 * or use "driver_override" in sysfs.
 	 */
+	{ .compatible = "turing,pi2-nodes" },
 	{}
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, gpio_aggregator_dt_ids);
